From: Darrel Griet <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 23:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] v10: Drop the redundant pre-set vsync wait on minnow

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [minnow command-mode panel specific]

swap() waited on the vsync callback before calling hwc_device->set().
On minnow's DSI command-mode panel that wait is redundant: the panel
latches from its own GRAM on its internal TE boundary and set() already
blocks until the commit completes (the retire fence is signalled by the
time set() returns, measured fence wait ~0 ms). The extra wait added
~7 ms of pure latency to the render thread's critical path each frame,
pushing wait+set (7+17 ms) past one vsync period so frames alternated
between 22 and 44 ms (~34 fps effective). Removing it lets set()'s own
TE sync pace the loop, giving a steady ~22 ms/frame (~44 fps, the
panel's refresh ceiling).

Instrumented swap() phase averages during a continuous animation:
  before: wall=29.1 wait=7.4 set=16.7 fence=0.0
  after:  wall=22.6 wait=0.0 set=17.4 fence=0.0

---
--- a/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_backend_v10.cpp
@@ -239,11 +239,16 @@
 {
     HWC_PLUGIN_ASSERT_ZERO(!(hwc_list->retireFenceFd == -1));
 
-    // Wait for vsync before posting new frame
-    // or force swap if exceeding the vsync timeframe
-    vsync_mutex.lock();
-    vsync_cond.wait(&vsync_mutex, 1000/vsyncFPS);
-    vsync_mutex.unlock();
+    // The Moto 360 panel is a DSI command-mode panel: it latches a new frame
+    // from its own GRAM only on its internal TE (tearing-effect) boundary, and
+    // hwc_device->set() below blocks until that commit completes (the retire
+    // fence is already signalled by the time set() returns). Waiting for the
+    // vsync callback here as well just added a whole extra ~7 ms of latency on
+    // the render thread's critical path per frame - pushing wait + set past one
+    // vsync period so frames alternated 22/44 ms (~34 fps). set()'s own TE sync
+    // paces us, so let it: dropping this wait yields a steady ~22 ms/frame
+    // (~44 fps, the panel's ceiling). This is safe only because the panel
+    // self-paces, hence a minnow-specific change.
 
     hwc_list->dpy = EGL_NO_DISPLAY;
     hwc_list->sur = EGL_NO_SURFACE;
